/T (For a finite graph with a visited set, each vertex is processed once and each edge is examined a bounded number of times. Its graph-search time is O\(V+E\), while the recursion stack is bounded by the depth of the active DFS path. This distinction explains why duplicate detection is essential in a hospital map containing cycles.)
