399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 81 0 R
/T (At one million locations, BFS generated and expanded all 1,000,000 vertices and reached a maximum frontier of 500,000. Recursive DFS found a route after 951,438 expansions and had a maximum active recursion depth proxy of 38 in this test. UCS expanded 619,203 vertices, generated 885,663 priority entries and reached a maximum heap size of 207,200. The queue/stack/heap values count active search entries, not measured RAM bytes. DFS records the maximum recursive call depth, while its visited and parent sets still consume O\(V\) memory.)
/E (At one million locations, BFS generated and expanded all 1,000,000 vertices and reached a maximum frontier of 500,000. Recursive DFS found a route after 951,438 expansions and had a maximum active recursion depth proxy of 38 in this test. UCS expanded 619,203 vertices, generated 885,663 priority entries and reached a maximum heap size of 207,200. The queue/stack/heap values count active search entries, not measured RAM bytes. DFS records the maximum recursive call depth, while its visited and parent sets still consume O\(V\) memory.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 81 0 R
/T (For the one-million-vertex graph, the five measured run times were: BFS 0.455, 0.431, 0.422, 0.426, 0.412 s; recursive DFS 0.479, 0.506, 0.515, 0.582, 0.575 s; UCS 4.612, 4.124, 4.176, 4.121, 4.566 s.)
