406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 82 0 R
/T (I recommend Uniform-Cost Search as the primary route planner for the stated weighted hospital graph. The performance measure includes travel time, and the edges have different non-negative costs. BFS minimizes the number of edges, which may choose a route with more travel time. DFS can find a route but offers no optimality guarantee. UCS expands locations in increasing accumulated travel cost and therefore returns a minimum-cost route under the stated assumptions.)
/E (I recommend Uniform-Cost Search as the primary route planner for the stated weighted hospital graph. The performance measure includes travel time, and the edges have different non-negative costs. BFS minimizes the number of edges, which may choose a route with more travel time. DFS can find a route but offers no optimality guarantee. UCS expands locations in increasing accumulated travel cost and therefore returns a minimum-cost route under the stated assumptions.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 82 0 R
/T (The recommendation is supported by the experiment: for the 1,000,000-location graph, UCS returned cost 87, compared with BFS cost 97 and DFS cost 121. UCS expanded 619,203 vertices, fewer than BFS \(1,000,000\) and DFS \(951,438\), but required 4.3199 seconds on average compared with 0.4291 seconds for BFS and 0.5315 seconds for DFS. This shows the trade-off: stronger route quality costs more computation.)
/E (The recommendation is supported by the experiment: for the 1,000,000-location graph, UCS returned cost 87, compared with BFS cost 97 and DFS cost 121. UCS expanded 619,203 vertices, fewer than BFS \(1,000,000\) and DFS \(951,438\), but required 4.3199 seconds on average compared with 0.4291 seconds for BFS and 0.5315 seconds for DFS. This shows the trade-off: stronger route quality costs more computation.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 82 0 R
/T (The graph preprocessing took about 0.8451 seconds at one million locations. It is a one-time cost if the map remains unchanged; if corridors or lifts change, the affected adjacency information must be updated. The main limitation is UCS priority-queue memory and runtime. A practical deployment should use a validated map, restrict edges to currently safe/available passages, monitor dynamic obstacles, and replan when the graph changes. For very large hospitals, hierarchical planning by building/wing/floor can reduce the active search region while retaining UCS within each region.)
/E (The graph preprocessing took about 0.8451 seconds at one million locations. It is a one-time cost if the map remains unchanged; if corridors or lifts change, the affected adjacency information must be updated. The main limitation is UCS priority-queue memory and runtime. A practical deployment should use a validated map, restrict edges to currently safe/available passages, monitor dynamic obstacles, and replan when the graph changes. For very large hospitals, hierarchical planning by building/wing/floor can reduce the active search region while retaining UCS within each region.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
