/T (uninformed strategies. Their behaviour differs in route quality, frontier storage and computation. For non-negative weighted travel-time edges, UCS is the most suitable of the three as the primary route optimizer, although its priority-queue cost must be managed. When localization becomes uncertain, the state must change from a single junction to a belief set. The recommended Day-4 response is to add local sensing and conditional planning, then use UCS from each sufficiently localized state.)
