/Title (BFS explores the graph level by level. It first visits the start location, then all locations one move away, then all locations two moves away, and so on. A FIFO queue preserves this order. A visited set prevents the robot planner from repeatedly adding the same junction when corridors form cycles.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1010 0 R
/Next 1025 0 R
>>
endobj
1018 0 obj
<<
/Title (Preprocessing: Convert the hospital map into adjacency lists. Initialize a visited set and parent map. This approach is selected because it is complete on a finite graph and finds a route with the fewest edges. Its limitation is that fewest edges need not mean minimum travel time when edge costs differ.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1010 0 R
/Prev 1025 0 R
>>
endobj
