/Title (The robot follows the acting rationally view of AI. It selects actions that are expected to achieve the goal while minimizing travel cost and respecting safety constraints. It is rational when it chooses the best action based on its percepts, map, available actions and performance measure; rationality does not mean that it must always know the future perfectly.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1015 0 R
/Next 1022 0 R
>>
endobj
1022 0 obj
<<
/Title (This is a classical problem-solving task from the early symbolic-AI tradition. Early AI systems represented a problem using states, operators and goals, then searched a state space for a sequence of actions. The hospital graph is a modern practical example of the same state-space search idea.)
