/Title (The recommendation is supported by the experiment: for the 1,000,000-location graph, UCS returned cost 87, compared with BFS cost 97 and DFS cost 121. UCS expanded 619,203 vertices, fewer than BFS \(1,000,000\) and DFS \(951,438\), but required 4.3199 seconds on average compared with 0.4291 seconds for BFS and 0.5315 seconds for DFS. This shows the trade-off: stronger route quality costs more computation.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1116 0 R
/Prev 1128 0 R
/Next 1142 0 R
>>
endobj
1142 0 obj
<<
/Title (The graph preprocessing took about 0.8451 seconds at one million locations. It is a one-time cost if the map remains unchanged; if corridors or lifts change, the affected adjacency information must be updated. The main limitation is UCS priority-queue memory and runtime. A practical deployment should use a validated map, restrict edges to currently safe/available passages, monitor dynamic obstacles, and replan when the graph changes. For very large hospitals, hierarchical planning by building/wing/floor can reduce the active search region while retaining UCS within each region.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1116 0 R
/Prev 1141 0 R
/Next 1129 0 R
>>
endobj
