/Title (To make the effect measurable, a small abstract test model is used. There are k possible leaf junctions. Each leaf has its own safe command that reaches the pharmacy docking point; a command intended for a different leaf is not guaranteed safe. Without a local sensor, no single first command is valid for all k candidates, so a guaranteed open-loop plan cannot be formed. With a perfect local sensor, the observation identifies the leaf and the robot follows the matching one-move route. Plan length counts one sensing step plus one movement step.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1144 0 R
/First 1165 0 R
/Last 1166 0 R
/Count -5
/Next 1167 0 R
>>
endobj
1156 0 obj
<<
/Title (Final decision: MODIFY the original design. Retain UCS as the route-cost optimizer, but do not use it from an assumed single start location after localization failure. First maintain and reduce the belief state using safe local sensing; then execute a conditional UCS route. This is safer and avoids blindly committing to a route that is valid for only one of the possible junctions.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1144 0 R
/Prev 1167 0 R
>>
endobj
